1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,960
[The D Dorm]

2
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:03,790
Ugh...

3
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:06,190
We still have eight rooms left unchecked.

4
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:08,360
I think Grandma Gaysorn's relative

5
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:09,790
must be in one of these rooms.

6
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:10,720
Mm, here...

7
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,620
Take this.

8
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:12,190
Here...

9
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:13,810
- Hey...
- Will you show up?

10
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:15,450
Whoa, whoa!

11
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:16,320
Calm down, Dobby.

12
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:17,290
What the hell are you doing?

13
00:00:17,290 --> 00:00:18,420
I'm torturing Grandpa.

14
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:20,240
He hasn't shown up for a few days.

15
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:21,790
I lit the incense, but got no answer.

16
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:22,990
Giving alms to the monk didn't work.

17
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:24,420
So I'm trying to...

18
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:25,580
provoke him,

19
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:26,450
in case he shows up.

20
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:28,770
Stop it.

21
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:30,440
He must have fainted by now.

22
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:32,590
Or did he reincarnate?

23
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:34,250
Hey, are you crazy?

24
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:35,580
He wouldn't reincarnate

25
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:37,140
since he hasn't met Grandma Gaysorn yet.

26
00:00:37,390 --> 00:00:38,410
Whoa, be more gentle with that...

27
00:00:38,590 --> 00:00:39,790
If that doesn't work,

28
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:41,120
I have another idea.

29
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:43,390
You have an important keepsake, right?

30
00:00:43,390 --> 00:00:44,740
Fine, then.

31
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:45,460
Move.

32
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:46,400
Mm.

33
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:50,140
Look!

34
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:53,730
Hey, go back to where you were.

35
00:00:53,730 --> 00:00:54,650
- Ugh, I have to be here, too...
- Yeah.

36
00:00:54,650 --> 00:00:55,390
Stand there.

37
00:00:55,390 --> 00:00:56,170
Hey!

38
00:00:56,330 --> 00:00:57,790
If you still don't show up,

39
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:00,620
I'm going to burn this powder bottle.

40
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:02,340
It's something you cherish, isn't it?

41
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:04,440
Will you come out or not?

42
00:01:04,849 --> 00:01:06,190
Will you come out?

43
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,080
Hey!

44
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:08,450
- You!
- Ow!

45
00:01:08,450 --> 00:01:09,789
What the hell are you doing?!

46
00:01:09,970 --> 00:01:11,810
This is Gramps' keepsake

47
00:01:11,810 --> 00:01:13,100
for when he misses his grandson.

48
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:15,789
[Little Cloud]

49
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:16,690
Wait...

50
00:01:16,690 --> 00:01:17,620
Gramps' grandson...

51
00:01:18,190 --> 00:01:19,280
That's you, isn't it?

52
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:22,700
Then the naked baby here...

53
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:23,580
is you?

54
00:01:24,190 --> 00:01:25,180
Do we look familiar?

55
00:01:25,970 --> 00:01:26,880
Yeah, you do.

56
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:30,000
You're in trouble, Dobby.

57
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:30,760
Now

58
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:31,960
Ms. Danis knows

59
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:33,680
that you're on the bottle.

60
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:34,620
And you have the nickname

61
00:01:34,759 --> 00:01:36,770
Little Eggy.

62
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:37,560
Hey...

63
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:38,930
- Why did you say that?
- Ow.

64
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:40,990
- Little Eggy.
- Hey.

65
00:01:40,990 --> 00:01:41,600
Little...

66
00:01:42,110 --> 00:01:43,390
Now everyone knows.

67
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:44,460
Hey,

68
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:45,620
can I ask you something?

69
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:46,120
What?

70
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,650
Don't tell anyone about this.

71
00:01:47,650 --> 00:01:48,420
It's embarrassing.

72
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:49,840
Don't worry,

73
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:51,789
everybody already knows.

74
00:01:51,789 --> 00:01:52,460
Huh?!

75
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:53,729
Well, Gramps

76
00:01:53,729 --> 00:01:55,860
went around and bragged to the entire dorm

77
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:57,530
that the boy on the bottle of powder

78
00:01:57,530 --> 00:01:58,650
is his grandson.

79
00:01:58,990 --> 00:01:59,690
See?

80
00:02:01,850 --> 00:02:02,440
Ugh...

81
00:02:02,590 --> 00:02:03,790
So, why are you here today?

82
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:05,620
I brought the documents
for you to sign.

83
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:07,780
And I'm going to leave today.

84
00:02:08,009 --> 00:02:09,009
Are you going to quit?

85
00:02:09,789 --> 00:02:12,010
I'm asking for personal leave!

86
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:13,640
My mother is sick today.

87
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:14,860
Hey, wait...

88
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:16,260
You're an orphan, aren't you?

89
00:02:17,460 --> 00:02:19,850
The kids at my orphanage

90
00:02:20,130 --> 00:02:20,860
call the director

91
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:22,320
"Mother."

92
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:23,970
I see.

93
00:02:24,410 --> 00:02:25,210
Okay, alright...

94
00:02:25,390 --> 00:02:25,960
You'd...

95
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:27,250
better go see her soon.

96
00:02:27,650 --> 00:02:28,610
Sign the documents

97
00:02:28,610 --> 00:02:30,190
by this evening.

98
00:02:30,930 --> 00:02:32,210
Little Eggy.

99
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,170
Little Eggy...

100
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:37,390
I'll tell Auntie Duang about this.

101
00:02:38,590 --> 00:02:39,790
Little Eggy.

102
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:40,760
Little... You little...

103
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:42,210
Dax, this is your fault.

104
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,620
- It's all because of you.
- Stop, stop...

105
00:02:43,620 --> 00:02:44,590
Hey, wait, one sec.

106
00:02:46,460 --> 00:02:46,990
Oh?

107
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:48,730
- Dax.
- Hm?

108
00:02:49,579 --> 00:02:50,940
Mr. Sompong texted me.

109
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:52,210
Little Eggy?

110
00:02:52,210 --> 00:02:52,990
No,

111
00:02:52,990 --> 00:02:53,810
take this seriously.

112
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:56,130
"Can we meet to discuss

113
00:02:56,130 --> 00:02:57,790
what we're going to do
about selling the dorm?"

114
00:02:57,790 --> 00:02:59,410
I've already put off the meeting about

115
00:02:59,410 --> 00:03:00,420
selling the dorm a few times.

116
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:03,790
Uh...

117
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:04,990
- Hey.
- Hm?

118
00:03:04,990 --> 00:03:05,890
Don't worry, Dobby.

119
00:03:06,330 --> 00:03:07,170
You've got me.

120
00:03:07,390 --> 00:03:09,060
Every solution has a problem.

121
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:10,440
Isn't it "Every problem has a solution"?

122
00:03:12,050 --> 00:03:12,940
Yeah, that one.

123
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:13,780
I don't want you to feel stressed.

124
00:03:14,050 --> 00:03:14,810
Little Eggy...

125
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:18,190
If you say that again, I'll slap you.

126
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:19,650
Do it on the left side.

127
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:30,990
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

128
00:03:32,990 --> 00:03:39,910
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

129
00:03:39,930 --> 00:03:45,829
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

130
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:53,660
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

131
00:03:54,430 --> 00:03:58,930
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

132
00:03:58,930 --> 00:04:02,580
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

133
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:06,170
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

134
00:04:06,170 --> 00:04:09,090
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

135
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:12,220
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

136
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:19,120
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

137
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:26,320
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

138
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:33,520
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

139
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:40,720
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫

140
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:44,590
[The D Dorm]

141
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:51,100
Mr. Sompong,

142
00:04:51,650 --> 00:04:53,760
I'm definitely going to sell the dorm,

143
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:55,620
but I'm having
some trouble with the tenants.

144
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:56,420
Well...

145
00:04:56,900 --> 00:04:57,790
most of them

146
00:04:57,980 --> 00:04:59,420
have year-long leases.

147
00:05:00,190 --> 00:05:01,060
If they don't leave,

148
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:02,590
there's nothing I can do.

149
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:04,760
Didn't you tell me

150
00:05:04,990 --> 00:05:06,440
you'd negotiate with them?

151
00:05:06,650 --> 00:05:08,590
I can't wait for a whole year.

152
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:10,440
How about this?

153
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:13,210
I'll go convince everyone to move out.

154
00:05:13,210 --> 00:05:14,180
I'm not leaving!

155
00:05:18,610 --> 00:05:19,730
How else will I make a living?

156
00:05:20,450 --> 00:05:20,960
Uh...

157
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,180
who are you?

158
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:23,440
That's

159
00:05:23,970 --> 00:05:25,600
one of the tenants in my dorm.

160
00:05:25,860 --> 00:05:26,880
He probably followed me.

161
00:05:27,050 --> 00:05:28,990
It's just a small square room,

162
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:34,880
but it's still precious to me!

163
00:05:35,930 --> 00:05:37,170
My memories

164
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:38,590
linger in every corner of the room!

165
00:05:39,170 --> 00:05:40,990
Ugh, I can't tell where this is going.

166
00:05:40,990 --> 00:05:41,730
Uh...

167
00:05:41,860 --> 00:05:42,920
can you elaborate?

168
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:43,850
Grandpa and Grandma

169
00:05:44,130 --> 00:05:45,260
are pounding on the balcony!

170
00:05:46,659 --> 00:05:47,290
Pound what?

171
00:05:47,420 --> 00:05:48,190
Betel quid.

172
00:05:48,190 --> 00:05:48,740
Phew...

173
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:50,960
Grandfather and Grandmother

174
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:52,080
are busy in the corner of the room!

175
00:05:53,170 --> 00:05:53,920
Busy doing what?

176
00:05:54,330 --> 00:05:55,080
Plucking gray hairs.

177
00:05:56,220 --> 00:05:57,300
Uncle and Auntie

178
00:05:57,300 --> 00:05:58,730
like it filthy!

179
00:05:58,730 --> 00:05:59,290
What?

180
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:00,190
Why?

181
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:00,940
They own a laundromat.

182
00:06:00,970 --> 00:06:01,920
Oh... Laundromat.

183
00:06:03,340 --> 00:06:03,690
Unkie...

184
00:06:04,060 --> 00:06:04,770
Aunty...

185
00:06:04,770 --> 00:06:06,040
Dad, and Mom...

186
00:06:06,190 --> 00:06:06,960
are going at it on the bed!

187
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:08,590
Go where?

188
00:06:08,590 --> 00:06:09,300
Go to sleep!

189
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:11,420
Poor thing.

190
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:13,390
Wait, wait, wait.

191
00:06:13,390 --> 00:06:15,790
Why are there so many people
in such a small room?

192
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:17,100
My room may be small,

193
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:18,740
but my thing is huge.

194
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:19,920
What's huge?

195
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:20,740
The memories I made.

196
00:06:22,060 --> 00:06:22,800
See?

197
00:06:22,990 --> 00:06:24,190
His memories are huge to him.

198
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:25,390
I don't care.

199
00:06:25,890 --> 00:06:26,590
I'm not leaving,

200
00:06:26,590 --> 00:06:28,250
no matter what!

201
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:30,570
You... What is this?

202
00:06:30,570 --> 00:06:31,240
Mr. Sompong,

203
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:32,200
let me handle this.

204
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:32,820
Hey...

205
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:33,790
- Mr. Dax!
- I'm not leaving!

206
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:34,840
Mr. Dax, calm down.

207
00:06:34,840 --> 00:06:35,490
Calm down.

208
00:06:35,490 --> 00:06:36,190
- Leave for now.
- No.

209
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:37,180
I'll talk to him.

210
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:38,090
Mr. Dax, please leave.

211
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:38,720
I'm not leaving.

212
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:39,420
Mr. Dax, calm down.

213
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:40,090
I'm not leaving.

214
00:06:40,090 --> 00:06:40,760
Mr. Dax!

215
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:42,570
Can you please calm down for a bit?

216
00:06:42,570 --> 00:06:43,210
No,

217
00:06:43,210 --> 00:06:43,850
I'm not leaving.

218
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:46,990
Mr. Sompong,

219
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:48,900
that was just one person.

220
00:06:49,090 --> 00:06:50,060
At the dorm...

221
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:51,610
there are problem tenants in more than ten rooms.

222
00:06:51,610 --> 00:06:52,300
Ten rooms?!

223
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:52,990
That's right.

224
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:54,490
Whoa, what should we do, then?

225
00:06:54,490 --> 00:06:56,960
My project can't be delayed any longer.

226
00:07:00,190 --> 00:07:01,090
Three months!

227
00:07:01,810 --> 00:07:03,140
Give me three months.

228
00:07:03,930 --> 00:07:06,720
I'll definitely get this dorm
ready for sale, Mr. Sompong.

229
00:07:08,130 --> 00:07:08,590
Alright.

230
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:11,820
But you have to
sign a contract with me this time.

231
00:07:12,190 --> 00:07:12,920
Of course.

232
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:17,130
Oh, the Feng Shui Master I told you about...

233
00:07:17,130 --> 00:07:18,190
- They will...
- Oh.

234
00:07:18,190 --> 00:07:19,100
Mr. Sompong,

235
00:07:19,250 --> 00:07:20,320
I don't think that's necessary.

236
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:22,440
You can bring him
here after three months.

237
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:24,450
Oh, I wanted to tell you that
I won't be bringing him here anymore.

238
00:07:24,450 --> 00:07:25,700
Oh, you won't?

239
00:07:25,700 --> 00:07:28,020
My boss will hire a shaman
to handle this instead.

240
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:28,800
Huh?!

241
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:29,970
A shaman?!

242
00:07:29,970 --> 00:07:30,440
Mm.

243
00:07:31,350 --> 00:07:32,250
When will he arrive?

244
00:07:32,590 --> 00:07:34,460
I heard he arrived a few days ago.

245
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:35,540
A few days ago?!

246
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:37,280
My boss picked him himself.

247
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:38,590
He's very talented.

248
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:41,540
He's sealed ghosts in pots countless times.

249
00:07:41,710 --> 00:07:43,100
Your grandpa already passed, right?

250
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:43,390
Yes.

251
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:44,970
This time, your grandpa will be...

252
00:07:44,990 --> 00:07:45,840
dead dead.

253
00:07:46,990 --> 00:07:48,190
Dead dead?

254
00:07:50,590 --> 00:07:51,620
Dead dead.

255
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:55,620
Was the reason Grandpa vanished...

256
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:57,010
because he was sealed in a pot...

257
00:07:57,010 --> 00:07:59,640
and he's now dead dead?!

258
00:08:00,450 --> 00:08:01,220
Grandpa.

259
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:02,400
Gramps, are you there?

260
00:08:02,590 --> 00:08:03,280
Grandpa.

261
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:04,990
Gramps, come out and see Dobby.

262
00:08:05,210 --> 00:08:05,970
Grandpa!

263
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:07,810
- Gramps!
- Grandpa!

264
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:10,990
Grandpa.

265
00:08:12,190 --> 00:08:12,680
What?

266
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,000
Grandpa, come out already.

267
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:15,790
Gramps.

268
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:16,990
Gramps.

269
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:20,590
Grandpa!

270
00:08:22,380 --> 00:08:23,200
Grandpa!

271
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:24,600
Hey, where did he go?

272
00:08:26,780 --> 00:08:28,240
- Gramps!
- Grandpa!

273
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:28,990
Gramps?

274
00:08:28,990 --> 00:08:30,000
- Grandpa!
- Gramps...

275
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,050
Gramps.

276
00:08:31,050 --> 00:08:31,850
Gramps?

277
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:33,250
Hey...

278
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:35,280
If he really was captured by the shaman,

279
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:36,419
wouldn't that be great?

280
00:08:36,559 --> 00:08:38,080
That way, you could sell this dorm.

281
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:41,919
How could I do that?

282
00:08:42,059 --> 00:08:43,620
I don't wanna break
the promise I made to him.

283
00:08:43,620 --> 00:08:44,100
Oh?

284
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:45,790
I want to keep my word.

285
00:08:45,790 --> 00:08:46,560
Hey,

286
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:47,440
that's suspicious.

287
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:48,190
