is none of your concern.

571
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:50,460
How could you say that?

572
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:51,790
My head still hurts even now.

573
00:17:51,970 --> 00:17:53,210
It obviously concerns me.

574
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:54,240
After you.

575
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:57,770
After...

576
00:17:57,790 --> 00:17:59,410
- Daeng, Daeng, Daeng, help me out.
- Oh.

577
00:18:01,530 --> 00:18:03,450
This way.

578
00:18:03,450 --> 00:18:04,250
Go downstairs.

579
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:04,990
Oh, wow...

580
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:07,760
They're leaving.

581
00:18:16,520 --> 00:18:17,660
Hey, wait.

582
00:18:17,660 --> 00:18:18,190
What?

583
00:18:18,330 --> 00:18:19,940
If this really is a shaman's room,

584
00:18:20,730 --> 00:18:21,790
we can't be too careful.

585
00:18:22,940 --> 00:18:24,810
A kuman thong might be targeting us.

586
00:18:25,390 --> 00:18:26,120
What should we do, then?

587
00:18:26,770 --> 00:18:27,220
Look.

588
00:18:31,250 --> 00:18:33,520
Let's play! Let's play!

589
00:18:33,790 --> 00:18:34,740
Let's play.

590
00:18:45,340 --> 00:18:46,220
Whoa...

591
00:18:46,410 --> 00:18:47,420
He's gone now.

592
00:18:48,770 --> 00:18:49,700
It's gone now, yeah.

593
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:50,590
You mean the kuman thong?

594
00:18:50,970 --> 00:18:52,010
Your braincells.

595
00:18:52,220 --> 00:18:52,990
They are all gone.

596
00:18:52,990 --> 00:18:53,730
Hey...

597
00:18:53,730 --> 00:18:54,930
- Ugh, this is stupid.
- You're being mean again...

598
00:18:58,990 --> 00:19:00,190
Hide inside.

599
00:19:16,850 --> 00:19:17,540
Whoa...

600
00:19:18,050 --> 00:19:18,740
Whoa...

601
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:29,770
Whoa...

602
00:19:30,570 --> 00:19:31,700
All these pots...

603
00:19:31,950 --> 00:19:34,100
If he wasn't a shaman, he'd make
a great hot pot restaurant owner.

604
00:19:37,390 --> 00:19:37,860
Hey,

605
00:19:38,480 --> 00:19:39,790
why are there only empty pots here?

606
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:41,970
If Grandpa's ghost was really in there,

607
00:19:42,490 --> 00:19:43,800
there must be a red talisman
over it, right?

608
00:19:45,180 --> 00:19:45,790
You're right.

609
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:47,400
Where is it, then?

610
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:00,500
Dax.

611
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:01,040
Whoa.

612
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:02,450
It's chained up.

613
00:20:05,970 --> 00:20:06,570
Hey...

614
00:20:06,770 --> 00:20:07,720
Move, move, move.

615
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:20,590
So, what's wrong with my car?

616
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:25,390
Well, our dorm has a new rule.

617
00:20:25,900 --> 00:20:28,090
Every tenant with a natural gas car

618
00:20:28,090 --> 00:20:30,970
must receive a safety training course

619
00:20:30,970 --> 00:20:32,640
hosted by me.

620
00:20:32,780 --> 00:20:33,450
Huh?!

621
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:34,740
What training course?

622
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:38,940
Without further ado, let's begin
our safety training course

623
00:20:38,940 --> 00:20:41,180
for natural gas car owners!

624
00:20:44,820 --> 00:20:46,640
To ensure safety for all tenants,

625
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:49,010
please follow these five Ds.

626
00:20:49,010 --> 00:20:50,020
The first D.

627
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:52,040
Do a sniff test before you start the car

628
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:53,440
in case there is a gas leak.

629
00:20:57,130 --> 00:20:57,790
What?

630
00:21:00,900 --> 00:21:01,820
What?

631
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:04,160
A gas leak!

632
00:21:05,210 --> 00:21:06,400
The second D.

633
00:21:06,770 --> 00:21:09,540
Do fasten your seatbelt before driving.

634
00:21:15,680 --> 00:21:16,990
I said fasten your seatbelt, not fishing.

635
00:21:16,990 --> 00:21:18,190
I have to pull it over my belly.

636
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:20,590
In case...

637
00:21:20,860 --> 00:21:21,440
the gas explodes.

638
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:22,410
Boom!

639
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:24,580
It will be easier to find your body.

640
00:21:29,620 --> 00:21:30,400
Everything remains intact.

641
00:21:32,060 --> 00:21:32,920
What even is this?

642
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:33,790
This is ridiculous.

643
00:21:34,530 --> 00:21:35,480
How is this ridiculous?

644
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:36,190
Come here.

645
00:21:37,580 --> 00:21:39,080
Sit here and you might
understand it better.

646
00:21:40,020 --> 00:21:41,840
Safety measures must not be overlooked.

647
00:21:44,920 --> 00:21:46,220
Sorry, but this is a car, not a bus.

648
00:21:46,220 --> 00:21:47,450
- Why are you holding the handle?
- I'm sorry.

649
00:21:48,190 --> 00:21:49,280
The third D.

650
00:21:49,280 --> 00:21:51,660
Do read dhamma books regularly,

651
00:21:51,660 --> 00:21:52,990
so you become more mindful

652
00:21:53,220 --> 00:21:55,390
and remain calm when you drive.

653
00:21:56,010 --> 00:21:57,450
Screech!

654
00:22:00,840 --> 00:22:01,690
Excuse me,

655
00:22:02,090 --> 00:22:03,300
why did you cut me off?

656
00:22:03,790 --> 00:22:04,990
I have a car insurance.

657
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:09,110
Sorry?

658
00:22:09,340 --> 00:22:10,400
Oh, we're Thai people.

659
00:22:10,530 --> 00:22:12,010
Let's greet one another with a warm hello,

660
00:22:12,190 --> 00:22:14,140
instead of a middle finger.

661
00:22:17,850 --> 00:22:18,730
Yes?

662
00:22:18,730 --> 00:22:19,390
My mom?

663
00:22:20,410 --> 00:22:21,240
I only have one mother.

664
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:22,540
Not six nor seven.

665
00:22:22,990 --> 00:22:23,760
Yes.

666
00:22:25,220 --> 00:22:26,130
This is nonsense.

667
00:22:26,130 --> 00:22:27,380
Such a waste of my time.

668
00:22:27,380 --> 00:22:28,440
Where are you going? The car is moving!

669
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:28,990
Oh, right.

670
00:22:29,740 --> 00:22:30,460
- Hey!
- What?

671
00:22:30,780 --> 00:22:31,900
You got me there.

672
00:22:33,790 --> 00:22:34,990
- What?
- What should we do?

673
00:22:35,100 --> 00:22:36,980
His patience ran out after only three Ds.

674
00:22:37,140 --> 00:22:40,100
We don't know if those
two Ds have found any evidence yet.

675
00:22:40,300 --> 00:22:41,340
They definitely don't have enough time.

676
00:22:41,340 --> 00:22:42,190
We have to stall him.

677
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:43,250
Mm.

678
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:45,400
Mr. Don,

679
00:22:45,900 --> 00:22:46,990
if you want to skip the course,

680
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:48,500
you'll have to prove that your car

681
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:50,590
is safe for the sake of our tenants.

682
00:22:50,590 --> 00:22:51,650
Prove what now?

683
00:22:51,650 --> 00:22:53,290
You've wasted enough of my time.

684
00:22:54,190 --> 00:22:55,080
We only ask for a moment.

685
00:22:55,390 --> 00:22:56,140
It won't take long.

686
00:22:57,460 --> 00:22:58,210
We'll take a look at your D.

687
00:22:58,210 --> 00:22:58,990
Whoa!

688
00:22:59,400 --> 00:23:00,190
We'll take a look at your "destiny."

689
00:23:01,240 --> 00:23:02,200
You scared me.

690
00:23:02,450 --> 00:23:03,340
It's an abbreviation, alright?

691
00:23:09,910 --> 00:23:10,670
Whoa!

692
00:23:11,450 --> 00:23:12,650
You're the real deal, huh?

693
00:23:13,650 --> 00:23:14,740
Where did you learn this from?

694
00:23:14,740 --> 00:23:15,360
I learned it...

695
00:23:15,360 --> 00:23:17,580
when I starred in
'Tawan Tud Burapa Withi.'

696
00:23:18,370 --> 00:23:19,390
You mean 'Tawan Tud Burapa'?

697
00:23:19,390 --> 00:23:20,250
This is the sequel.

698
00:23:20,450 --> 00:23:22,990
The lead died while he was
driving on Burapha Withi Expressway.

699
00:23:22,990 --> 00:23:24,500
He was shot. Bang! Bang! Bang!

700
00:23:24,500 --> 00:23:25,280
A bunch of bullet holes.

701
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:26,590
Whoa... That doesn't sound like a good movie.

702
00:23:27,240 --> 00:23:27,640
It is good, though.

703
00:23:27,640 --> 00:23:28,260
Yeah, whatever.

704
00:23:28,260 --> 00:23:28,850
Go!

705
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:44,220
Dax,

706
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:45,790
there are so many pots.

707
00:23:47,320 --> 00:23:48,190
Grandpa.

708
00:23:49,210 --> 00:23:49,960
Grandpa?

709
00:23:50,250 --> 00:23:50,970
Grandpa...

710
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:52,400
- Dax...
- Whoa.

711
00:23:53,240 --> 00:23:54,190
Grandpa isn't answering.

712
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:57,580
I'll...

713
00:23:57,580 --> 00:23:58,530
open every single one, then.

714
00:23:58,530 --> 00:23:59,610
Hey, wait, Dobby.

715
00:23:59,820 --> 00:24:00,190
Huh?

716
00:24:00,890 --> 00:24:01,850
If you opened them all,

717
00:24:02,590 --> 00:24:03,570
the D Dorm

718
00:24:03,790 --> 00:24:04,990
would turn into
Disneyland's Haunted Mansion.

719
00:24:06,580 --> 00:24:07,440
What should we do, then?

720
00:24:09,080 --> 00:24:09,790
Hey...

721
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:10,410
Hm?

722
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:11,700
You're Gramps' grandson.

723
00:24:13,100 --> 00:24:14,120
You have to use this.

724
00:24:14,960 --> 00:24:15,520
Here.

725
00:24:20,280 --> 00:24:20,720
My nipple?

726
00:24:20,720 --> 00:24:21,300
Ugh...

727
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:22,260
Your heart!

728
00:24:23,210 --> 00:24:24,190
Oh, my heart.

729
00:24:24,190 --> 00:24:25,120
- Yeah.
- Mm.

730
00:24:25,700 --> 00:24:26,590
Listen.

731
00:24:27,020 --> 00:24:27,380
Yeah?

732
00:24:27,980 --> 00:24:29,700
Back when I was studying acting,

733
00:24:31,010 --> 00:24:32,220
I learned that you could tell

734
00:24:33,130 --> 00:24:34,680
what color the other person
was thinking of

735
00:24:34,990 --> 00:24:36,440
just by holding hands with them.

736
00:24:38,410 --> 00:24:39,680
Try to focus.

737
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:40,160
Mm.

738
00:24:40,160 --> 00:24:41,250
Think of Gramps.

739
00:24:43,050 --> 00:24:44,590
You might be able to sense his presence.

740
00:24:46,010 --> 00:24:46,690
That...

741
00:24:46,990 --> 00:24:47,560
is...

742
00:24:48,190 --> 00:24:48,890
possible...

743
00:24:49,390 --> 00:24:50,260
Thank you, Ryu.

744
00:24:51,330 --> 00:24:51,790
It's Dax!

745
00:24:52,370 --> 00:24:52,990
Oh, Dax.

746
00:24:52,990 --> 00:24:53,730
- Mm.
- Alright.

747
00:25:10,140 --> 00:25:12,330
Are you hiding a secret?

748
00:25:15,680 --> 00:25:16,780
The cards are telling me that...

749
00:25:17,420 --> 00:25:20,020
you're covering up a mistake.

750
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:22,220
And the rotten filth

751
00:25:22,740 --> 00:25:24,190
you've been hiding

752
00:25:24,500 --> 00:25:25,570
will be exposed in no time.

753
00:25:28,140 --> 00:25:28,820
Mr. Don,

754
00:25:28,970 --> 00:25:30,620
are you really hiding something?

755
00:25:31,580 --> 00:25:32,820
Whatever it is that I'm hiding

756
00:25:33,060 --> 00:25:34,420
is none of your concern.

757
00:25:36,060 --> 00:25:37,390
But the cards told me.

758
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:40,990
You're breaking the law,

759
00:25:41,410 --> 00:25:42,560
the law of nature.

760
00:25:43,760 --> 00:25:44,590
Enough of this!

761
00:25:44,590 --> 00:25:45,920
- This is stupid. I'm going back to my room.
- Hey! Sit down!

762
00:25:46,040 --> 00:25:46,990
Don't go!

763
00:25:48,530 --> 00:25:49,620
You can't leave yet.

764
00:25:49,620 --> 00:25:51,440
If you insist on skipping the course,

765
00:25:51,440 --> 00:25:52,700
you'll have to see the D!

766
00:25:52,700 --> 00:25:53,380
- Huh?
- Destiny.

767
00:25:53,980 --> 00:25:54,440
Oh,

768
00:25:54,440 --> 00:25:55,170
a reading of your destiny!

769
00:25:55,950 --> 00:25:56,660
Don't try to stop me!

770
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:57,200
Sit!

771
00:25:57,200 --> 00:25:57,790
Stop.

772
00:25:57,790 --> 00:25:58,420
Sit down.

773
00:25:59,370 --> 00:26:00,620
If you want to stay safe,

774
00:26:00,620 --> 00:26:01,390
sit down,

775
00:26:01,530 --> 00:26:02,960
and let the cards guide you.

776
00:26:03,980 --> 00:26:04,820
Daeng the Handyman, hold him still!

777
00:26:04,820 --> 00:26:05,250
Hey,

778
00:26:07,120 --> 00:26:07,940
stop it!

779
00:26:08,180 --> 00:26:09,140
Don't forget your promise

780
00:26:09,140 --> 00:26:11,480
that you'll help me hold hands with your brother.

781
00:26:11,480 --> 00:26:12,190
Ugh, alright.

782
00:26:12,190 --> 00:26:13,390
Why are you nagging me so much?

783
00:26:13,390 --> 00:26:14,420
Try to stop him first.

784
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:16,420
You won't let me go, huh?

785
00:26:17,370 --> 00:26:18,440
Hey, he's going to use black magic!

786
00:26:18,440 --> 00:26:19,020
- Whoa.
- Whoa.

787
00:26:19,200 --> 00:26:20,850
Hey... What is he doing?

788
00:26:21,050 --> 00:26:21,790
- Stand back.
- Whoa.

789
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:25,240
He might be a master thief

790
00:26:25,240 --> 00:26:26,400
who practices black magic,

791
00:26:26,650 --> 00:26:27,680
but don't worry,

792
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:29,430
I know a few tricks that can protect us.

793
00:26:31,810 --> 00:26:32,590
You want some of this?

794
00:26:34,090 --> 00:26:34,370
Ow!

795
00:26:34,640 --> 00:26:34,990
Ow!

796
00:26:39,560 --> 00:26:40,120
What's wrong?

797
00:26:40,660 --> 00:26:42,020
It hurts, obviously.

798
00:26:42,020 --> 00:26:43,200
- Try again.
- Give it another try.

799
00:26:43,200 --> 00:26:44,170
Ohm... Tapati Tapata...

800
00:26:44,170 --> 00:26:45,340
- What now?!
- Ouch!

801
00:26:45,340 --> 00:26:46,450
Ugh, I'm leaving.

802
00:26:46,620 --> 00:26:47,220
Whoa.

803
00:26:48,730 --> 00:26:49,390
Ow!

804
00:26:52,220 --> 00:26:54,190
[The D Dorm]

805
00:26:54,800 --> 00:26:55,650
Grandpa.

806
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:57,940
Grandpa...

807
00:26:59,620 --> 00:27:01,180
If you can hear me,

808
00:27:01,180 --> 00:27:02,590
please say something.

809
00:27:03,790 --> 00:27:04,780
Vroom, vroom.

810
00:27:06,930 --> 00:27:07,580
Grandpa?

811
00:27:07,690 --> 00:27:08,590
Are you driving?

812
00:27:09,370 --> 00:27:10,120
Grandpa...

813
00:27:11,850 --> 00:27:13,180
- To the left, to the left.
- Dax!

814
00:27:13,850 --> 00:27:14,840
- Go that way...
- Dax,

815
00:27:14,840 --> 00:27:16,180
what the hell are you doing? Get in here!

816
00:27:18,190 --> 00:27:19,570
What were you doing?

817
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:20,760
Huh?

818
00:27:23,450 --> 00:27:24,190
Yeah, Guard Dum?

819
00:27:25,060 --> 00:27:25,920
- Huh?!
- Hah?!

820
00:27:26,510 --> 00:27:27,410
Don is on his way back here?

821
00:27:27,410 --> 00:27:28,120
What?

822
00:27:33,260 --> 00:27:34,990
Who put this R/C car here?

823
00:27:45,900 --> 00:27:47,400
What was that all about...?

824
00:27:50,920 --> 00:27:51,640
Huh?!

825
00:27:52,370 --> 00:27:53,400
Who's in here?!

826
00:27:55,080 --> 00:27:56,030
Show yourself!

827
00:28:05,250 --> 00:28:05,930
Come on out!

828
00:28:09,790 --> 00:28:10,660
Keep quiet...

829
00:28:16,990 --> 00:28:18,190
You're in there, huh?

830
00:28:30,350 --> 00:28:31,550
They must be in here...

831
00:28:46,040 --> 00:28:46,760
Hello?

832
00:28:46,990 --> 00:28:47,840
Gramps?

833
00:28:49,690 --> 00:28:51,110
I handled that already.

834
00:28:52,740 --> 00:28:53,250
Dobby...

835
00:28:53,810 --> 00:28:54,730
He's talking about Gramps.

836
00:28:54,940 --> 00:28:55,780
I heard that.

837
00:28:57,940 --> 00:28:59,100
Oh, you've arrived?

838
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:01,810
I'll bring it to you myself.

839
00:29:11,450 --> 00:29:13,020
This ends here, Gramps.

840
00:29:13,570 --> 00:29:14,250
Grandpa.

841
00:29:18,600 --> 00:29:19,390
Stop right there.

842
00:29:19,810 --> 00:29:21,080
- Whoa.
- Give me back my grandpa!

843
00:29:21,080 --> 00:29:22,280
Hey, how did you get in here?!

844
00:29:22,450 --> 00:29:23,140
You're evil.

845
00:29:23,140 --> 00:29:24,540
How dare you take his grandpa
away from him?

846
00:29:24,540 --> 00:29:25,700
What are you saying?!

847
00:29:25,700 --> 00:29:26,940
- Don't try to act innocent. Give him back to me!
- Hey!

848
00:29:26,940 --> 00:29:28,000
- Ow.
- Ouch.

849
00:29:28,140 --> 00:29:28,680
Hey!

850
00:29:31,540 --> 00:29:32,530
Hey, stop right there!

851
00:29:33,790 --> 00:29:34,990
- Stop it, you thief.
- Stop.

852
00:29:35,170 --> 00:29:36,190
What thief?!

853
00:29:36,190 --> 00:29:37,120
Hey, stop.

854
00:29:37,640 --> 00:29:38,440
Whoa, whoa.

855
00:29:41,420 --> 00:29:42,700
Give me back Grandpa's pot.

856
00:29:42,700 --> 00:29:43,750
Never!

857
00:29:45,940 --> 00:29:47,040
Don't try to run away.

858
00:29:50,930 --> 00:29:51,440
Whoa!

859
00:29:54,850 --> 00:29:55,650
Whoa, Dax.

860
00:29:56,120 --> 00:29:56,740
- Whoa.
- Whoa.

861
00:29:58,450 --> 00:29:58,990
Whoa.

862
00:30:02,720 --> 00:30:03,790
Let go!

863
00:30:04,240 --> 00:30:05,320
No... I won't.

864
00:30:05,320 --> 00:30:05,970
Let go...

865
00:30:06,190 --> 00:30:06,890
No.

866
00:30:06,890 --> 00:30:07,390
Let go.

867
00:30:07,970 --> 00:30:09,060
Give me the pot!

868
00:30:09,360 --> 00:30:10,200
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

869
00:30:10,800 --> 00:30:12,190
How about Virgil van Dijk's
defending style?

870
00:30:22,140 --> 00:30:22,770
What?

871
00:30:26,840 --> 00:30:27,480
- Ouch!
- Hey.

872
00:30:28,200 --> 00:30:29,050
Virgil van Dijk is now exhausted!

873
00:30:29,100 --> 00:30:30,190
This is why Liverpool
wasn't the champion!

874
00:30:30,190 --> 00:30:31,440
Ow, that hurts...

875
00:30:32,590 --> 00:30:33,460
- Hey.
- Don't try to run away.

876
00:30:34,180 --> 00:30:34,990
- Oh!
- Give me that.

877
00:30:40,580 --> 00:30:41,770
Whoa!

878
00:30:47,740 --> 00:30:49,640
Whoa...

879
00:30:52,680 --> 00:30:54,420
Grandpa!

880
00:31:02,730 --> 00:31:04,180
This is fermented fish!

881
00:31:05,840 --> 00:31:08,700
What are you doing?!

882
00:31:17,200 --> 00:31:17,960
Hey, Mr. Don,

883
00:31:18,190 --> 00:31:20,590
have you been making and
selling fermented fish here in this dorm?

884
00:31:22,210 --> 00:31:22,990
I'm sorry.

885
00:31:23,470 --> 00:31:26,400
[Don, occupation: (fermented fish) seller]

886
00:31:26,860 --> 00:31:27,790
If you were making fermented fish,

887
00:31:28,370 --> 00:31:30,190
then why is your room
full of sacred items?

888
00:31:30,190 --> 00:31:31,390
You were acting like a shaman, even.

889
00:31:32,100 --> 00:31:34,320
Well... I wanted my brand to stand out.

890
00:31:34,640 --> 00:31:36,440
And my friend said that

891
00:31:36,440 --> 00:31:38,510
I looked like Master
from 'Khemjira The Series.'

892
00:31:39,300 --> 00:31:40,720
So I turned that idea...

893
00:31:40,960 --> 00:31:41,810
into Master's fermented fish.

894
00:31:41,810 --> 00:31:43,020
- Whoa.
- Hmm.

895
00:31:43,020 --> 00:31:44,260
There are many other series
to choose from,

896
00:31:44,410 --> 00:31:45,240
why this one?

897
00:31:45,570 --> 00:31:47,290
Well, I like it.

898
00:31:47,330 --> 00:31:49,690
And what I like is none of your concern.

899
00:31:50,010 --> 00:31:51,000
Ooh...

900
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:52,050
Still feisty, huh?

901
00:31:52,050 --> 00:31:53,780
He's probably telling you...

902
00:31:53,780 --> 00:31:54,620
to keep your nose out of this.

903
00:31:55,610 --> 00:31:57,980
I almost asked him if he also
watched 'Your Third Series.'

904
00:31:58,990 --> 00:31:59,930
Don't forget to watch it as well.

905
00:32:00,580 --> 00:32:01,390
But wait,

906
00:32:01,980 --> 00:32:03,790
