1017
00:36:14,260 --> 00:36:15,640
- Oh.
- Ugh...

1018
00:36:15,790 --> 00:36:17,420
I only drew a mustache, though?

1019
00:36:18,170 --> 00:36:19,040
But look at me.

1020
00:36:19,260 --> 00:36:21,180
You drew all over my face.

1021
00:36:21,650 --> 00:36:23,200
- Just saying it makes me angry.
- And?

1022
00:36:23,200 --> 00:36:23,960
Give it to me...

1023
00:36:24,730 --> 00:36:25,880
Boys, stop...

1024
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:28,540
- That's enough.
- Let go.

1025
00:36:28,540 --> 00:36:29,450
- Let go.
- Ow.

1026
00:36:29,450 --> 00:36:30,190
Let go already.

1027
00:36:30,480 --> 00:36:31,850
- Stop fighting!
- Stop.

1028
00:36:31,850 --> 00:36:32,590
Dollar...

1029
00:36:32,590 --> 00:36:33,410
Let go, Dolly.

1030
00:36:33,410 --> 00:36:34,100
Let go.

1031
00:36:34,540 --> 00:36:35,530
- Stop this already.
- Dolly, let go.

1032
00:36:35,700 --> 00:36:36,530
Ugh, boys!

1033
00:36:37,390 --> 00:36:38,590
That's enough.

1034
00:36:38,890 --> 00:36:39,790
- Whoa!
- Huh!

1035
00:36:39,940 --> 00:36:40,560
Mom!

1036
00:36:40,560 --> 00:36:41,260
What happened?

1037
00:36:41,370 --> 00:36:42,380
You had to ask?

1038
00:36:42,760 --> 00:36:44,160
We're not going to that buffet anymore.

1039
00:36:44,380 --> 00:36:45,600
We're going to the salon

1040
00:36:45,600 --> 00:36:46,720
to wash all of this off.

1041
00:36:47,540 --> 00:36:48,620
- You...
- Go!

1042
00:36:49,240 --> 00:36:49,930
Quickly!

1043
00:36:50,800 --> 00:36:51,440
- Oh.
- Oh...

1044
00:36:51,580 --> 00:36:52,010
Whoa.

1045
00:36:52,010 --> 00:36:53,160
Whoa, Mom.

1046
00:36:53,160 --> 00:36:54,580
- He's so dramatic.
- You have a problem with that?

1047
00:36:55,390 --> 00:36:56,000
Go!

1048
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:58,450
Why did you draw a cross on my face?
This isn't an election.

1049
00:37:22,130 --> 00:37:22,850
Who are you?

1050
00:37:22,850 --> 00:37:23,410
Oh!

1051
00:37:23,540 --> 00:37:24,960
What are you doing here?

1052
00:37:25,740 --> 00:37:26,590
I...

1053
00:37:27,020 --> 00:37:27,790
Uh...

1054
00:37:28,040 --> 00:37:28,640
I...

1055
00:37:29,460 --> 00:37:30,520
I came to see my relative.

1056
00:37:32,820 --> 00:37:34,230
My relative is the owner of this restaurant.

1057
00:37:34,990 --> 00:37:36,010
Wait.

1058
00:37:37,080 --> 00:37:39,480
Weren't you the one spying on
Auntie Duang this afternoon?

1059
00:37:39,630 --> 00:37:40,620
Oh, oops...

1060
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:42,690
You have a great memory, huh?

1061
00:37:42,690 --> 00:37:44,170
Uh, well...

1062
00:37:44,340 --> 00:37:45,050
I...

1063
00:37:45,050 --> 00:37:47,290
I'm here to surprise them.

1064
00:37:49,160 --> 00:37:49,840
Well,

1065
00:37:49,840 --> 00:37:50,590
I...

1066
00:37:50,770 --> 00:37:51,300
I...

1067
00:37:51,300 --> 00:37:52,820
haven't seen them in a long time.

1068
00:37:52,820 --> 00:37:53,980
So...

1069
00:37:54,190 --> 00:37:55,220
I wanted to...

1070
00:37:55,220 --> 00:37:56,320
I want this reunion...

1071
00:37:56,320 --> 00:37:57,520
to be something...

1072
00:37:57,520 --> 00:37:58,560
special.

1073
00:37:58,990 --> 00:37:59,580
Yeah.

1074
00:38:03,790 --> 00:38:05,200
You were the one who told me

1075
00:38:05,200 --> 00:38:06,660
if I wanted to know
what Dad looks like,

1076
00:38:06,660 --> 00:38:08,410
just draw a mustache on him.

1077
00:38:14,330 --> 00:38:15,640
Don't tell me you are...

1078
00:38:16,810 --> 00:38:18,190
Auntie Duang's husband?

1079
00:38:18,500 --> 00:38:19,220
Whoa!

1080
00:38:21,570 --> 00:38:22,260
No, no, no, no.

1081
00:38:22,260 --> 00:38:22,990
That's wonderful.

1082
00:38:23,340 --> 00:38:24,890
Dolly will finally meet his father.

1083
00:38:25,850 --> 00:38:26,440
Shh.

1084
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:27,440
Keep quiet.

1085
00:38:27,440 --> 00:38:28,810
Yeah, I'm his father.

1086
00:38:28,880 --> 00:38:30,410
That's great, isn't it?

1087
00:38:30,770 --> 00:38:33,250
Dolly's family will finally be reunited.

1088
00:38:33,790 --> 00:38:35,370
Let me call him.

1089
00:38:35,370 --> 00:38:37,000
Whoa, no! Stop!

1090
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:37,740
Stop, stop.

1091
00:38:37,740 --> 00:38:38,240
Don't do that.

1092
00:38:38,540 --> 00:38:39,250
Don't call him.

1093
00:38:39,420 --> 00:38:40,450
Why not?

1094
00:38:40,990 --> 00:38:42,420
Well... Uh...

1095
00:38:43,170 --> 00:38:43,860
I...

1096
00:38:44,120 --> 00:38:46,000
I want it to be a surprise. Yeah.

1097
00:38:47,200 --> 00:38:48,730
Oh...

1098
00:38:49,390 --> 00:38:50,440
I get it now.

1099
00:38:51,650 --> 00:38:53,210
I'm jealous.

1100
00:38:53,480 --> 00:38:56,020
I wish I could have a
family moment like this, too

1101
00:38:58,270 --> 00:39:00,600
Let me know if you need anything.

1102
00:39:00,980 --> 00:39:02,800
I will gladly help.

1103
00:39:03,940 --> 00:39:04,740
Anything at all?

1104
00:39:06,390 --> 00:39:06,960
Here.

1105
00:39:07,260 --> 00:39:08,360
I took everything out.

1106
00:39:08,590 --> 00:39:09,790
Now...

1107
00:39:10,680 --> 00:39:12,190
Put this on.

1108
00:39:12,640 --> 00:39:14,280
Mm...

1109
00:39:15,420 --> 00:39:16,240
Good...

1110
00:39:21,120 --> 00:39:23,870
[The D Dorm]

1111
00:39:25,120 --> 00:39:26,890
The salon was closed,

1112
00:39:27,610 --> 00:39:30,060
and the hot pot restaurant
wouldn't let us inside.

1113
00:39:30,060 --> 00:39:32,410
This is all because of you two,
Dollar and Dolly.

1114
00:39:32,590 --> 00:39:33,210
Hey...

1115
00:39:33,210 --> 00:39:35,400
Could it be because of your clothes
that they didn't let us in?

1116
00:39:37,780 --> 00:39:38,400
- Hey.
- Mom.

1117
00:39:38,400 --> 00:39:38,880
Hm?

1118
00:39:39,240 --> 00:39:40,400
Why didn't you lock the door?

1119
00:39:42,060 --> 00:39:42,720
I did.

1120
00:39:43,390 --> 00:39:44,260
You didn't.

1121
00:39:44,590 --> 00:39:45,100
Oh, no.

1122
00:39:45,600 --> 00:39:46,300
What do we do now?

1123
00:39:48,810 --> 00:39:49,680
Be careful...

1124
00:39:54,400 --> 00:39:56,200
- Whoa!
- Ta-da!

1125
00:39:56,200 --> 00:39:57,640
This is a robbery.

1126
00:40:02,740 --> 00:40:04,380
Turn the lights on.

1127
00:40:04,380 --> 00:40:05,260
Ow...

1128
00:40:05,260 --> 00:40:06,560
- It's me.
- Who is it?

1129
00:40:06,560 --> 00:40:07,820
Who?

1130
00:40:07,820 --> 00:40:08,840
It's Dew.

1131
00:40:08,970 --> 00:40:10,070
Dew?!

1132
00:40:10,440 --> 00:40:11,160
Yes, it's me.

1133
00:40:11,160 --> 00:40:11,600
What?

1134
00:40:12,190 --> 00:40:13,090
Wait.

1135
00:40:13,640 --> 00:40:15,370
- Everything is gone.
- I'm sorry.

1136
00:40:15,370 --> 00:40:16,290
Don't tell me...

1137
00:40:16,590 --> 00:40:18,180
Did you rob my restaurant?

1138
00:40:18,460 --> 00:40:19,390
No,

1139
00:40:19,770 --> 00:40:21,790
I have a surprise for you.

1140
00:40:21,790 --> 00:40:22,280
Huh?

1141
00:40:23,160 --> 00:40:23,930
What surprise?

1142
00:40:26,050 --> 00:40:27,170
Let me go over it again.

1143
00:40:27,170 --> 00:40:27,790
Go on.

1144
00:40:28,040 --> 00:40:30,900
We'll surprise them by
tricking them that I'm a thief.

1145
00:40:30,900 --> 00:40:31,390
Yeah.

1146
00:40:31,580 --> 00:40:33,050
- And you'll come in to help me.
- Yes.

1147
00:40:33,050 --> 00:40:33,980
Like a superhero, right?

1148
00:40:33,980 --> 00:40:34,660
That's right.

1149
00:40:35,360 --> 00:40:37,860
Will this really impress them?

1150
00:40:37,860 --> 00:40:39,220
Of course it will.

1151
00:40:39,900 --> 00:40:40,810
Think of it like this,

1152
00:40:40,810 --> 00:40:43,890
I haven't seen my family in a long time,

1153
00:40:44,410 --> 00:40:45,420
and then suddenly

1154
00:40:45,740 --> 00:40:47,420
I show up to protect them.

1155
00:40:48,040 --> 00:40:48,970
Think about it.

1156
00:40:49,390 --> 00:40:53,610
They would be proud to have me
as the head of the family,

1157
00:40:53,610 --> 00:40:54,190
right?

1158
00:40:54,690 --> 00:40:55,610
Oh.

1159
00:40:55,610 --> 00:40:56,280
Yeah.

1160
00:40:56,280 --> 00:40:57,200
I get it now.

1161
00:40:57,320 --> 00:40:58,060
Yeah.

1162
00:40:58,080 --> 00:40:59,280
Don't worry,

1163
00:40:59,940 --> 00:41:02,670
I’ll do my best as a thief.

1164
00:41:02,780 --> 00:41:04,120
That's great. Yeah.

1165
00:41:06,620 --> 00:41:07,610
Uncle,

1166
00:41:08,290 --> 00:41:09,320
where are you?

1167
00:41:09,610 --> 00:41:10,090
What?

1168
00:41:10,320 --> 00:41:10,780
Wait...

1169
00:41:10,990 --> 00:41:12,190
Who are you talking to?

1170
00:41:12,660 --> 00:41:13,900
Your husband.

1171
00:41:14,010 --> 00:41:14,880
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

1172
00:41:15,370 --> 00:41:15,790
What?

1173
00:41:16,170 --> 00:41:17,520
Where is my dad, Dew?

1174
00:41:17,560 --> 00:41:18,190
Dad?

1175
00:41:19,440 --> 00:41:20,590
Uncle,

1176
00:41:20,860 --> 00:41:22,090
no need to hide anymore.

1177
00:41:23,130 --> 00:41:24,660
You can come out now, Uncle Wit.

1178
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:25,720
Wait.

1179
00:41:26,120 --> 00:41:26,860
Uncle Wit?

1180
00:41:27,240 --> 00:41:28,120
- Mm.
- Who is that?

1181
00:41:28,520 --> 00:41:30,190
My husband's name is Michael.

1182
00:41:30,530 --> 00:41:31,040
Huh?

1183
00:41:31,260 --> 00:41:32,000
Yes!

1184
00:41:35,860 --> 00:41:37,390
He isn't your husband?

1185
00:41:41,330 --> 00:41:42,010
He looks familiar.

1186
00:41:42,300 --> 00:41:42,900
Let me see.

1187
00:41:45,570 --> 00:41:46,140
No.

1188
00:41:46,140 --> 00:41:46,990
I know.

1189
00:41:47,960 --> 00:41:48,810
He’s the thief

1190
00:41:49,040 --> 00:41:50,590
that the police are after.

1191
00:41:50,770 --> 00:41:51,840
["WANTED" Royal Thai Police,
Mr. Wit Tulrat, Age: 47 Years Old]

1192
00:41:51,860 --> 00:41:53,540
[Arrest Warrant:
Residential Burglary]

1193
00:41:53,730 --> 00:41:55,110
- Hey...
- Dew,

1194
00:41:55,800 --> 00:41:56,590
don't tell me...

1195
00:41:57,010 --> 00:41:58,850
you brought a thief here
to rob my restaurant?

1196
00:41:58,850 --> 00:41:59,800
Oh, goodness.

1197
00:41:59,800 --> 00:42:00,520
I'm going to faint...

1198
00:42:00,520 --> 00:42:01,880
- Mom, Mom.
- Mom.

1199
00:42:02,170 --> 00:42:03,450
It's okay, Mom.

1200
00:42:06,300 --> 00:42:07,390
It burns.

1201
00:42:07,390 --> 00:42:08,380
Please do not hurt me.

1202
00:42:08,590 --> 00:42:10,700
Please do not hurt me!

1203
00:42:10,700 --> 00:42:12,080
Take that!

1204
00:42:12,080 --> 00:42:13,760
Stop! It burns!

1205
00:42:13,760 --> 00:42:14,960
- Stop right there!
- Are you challenging me?

1206
00:42:14,960 --> 00:42:16,480
- Stop!
- Take my ritual knife.

1207
00:42:16,480 --> 00:42:17,540
- Here.
- I am scared.

1208
00:42:17,570 --> 00:42:17,970
Stop.

1209
00:42:17,970 --> 00:42:18,960
Grandpa, I'm here to help you.

1210
00:42:21,610 --> 00:42:22,420
How dare you hurt Grandpa?

1211
00:42:23,180 --> 00:42:23,640
- Go.
- Wait.

1212
00:42:23,980 --> 00:42:25,210
Hey, wait, wait.

1213
00:42:25,210 --> 00:42:25,810
Hey...

1214
00:42:25,860 --> 00:42:26,900
This is a misunderstanding.

1215
00:42:26,900 --> 00:42:27,790
Dobby, Dobby.

1216
00:42:28,600 --> 00:42:29,600
Dobby!

1217
00:42:30,050 --> 00:42:31,890
Dobby, stop!

1218
00:42:31,890 --> 00:42:32,460
How could I stop?

1219
00:42:32,460 --> 00:42:33,380
He hurt you this badly!

1220
00:42:33,380 --> 00:42:33,970
Yeah!

1221
00:42:35,180 --> 00:42:38,060
Tong used to be my neighbor!

1222
00:42:40,880 --> 00:42:41,570
He's your friend?

1223
00:42:41,570 --> 00:42:42,850
We used to be neighbors,

1224
00:42:42,850 --> 00:42:44,100
and we were very close.

1225
00:42:45,790 --> 00:42:46,280
Dobby...

1226
00:42:46,700 --> 00:42:47,260
Tong...

1227
00:42:47,420 --> 00:42:47,980
Dobby...

1228
00:42:48,330 --> 00:42:50,180
Why didn't you say anything earlier?

1229
00:42:50,180 --> 00:42:51,200
This way.

1230
00:42:52,820 --> 00:42:53,540
Ugh...

1231
00:42:54,110 --> 00:42:55,390
Your grandsons weren't

1232
00:42:55,600 --> 00:42:56,590
holding back, huh?

1233
00:42:57,410 --> 00:42:58,160
I'm sorry.

1234
00:43:00,560 --> 00:43:01,180
Dobby...

1235
00:43:01,570 --> 00:43:03,490
So the shaman is Gramps' friend?

1236
00:43:06,520 --> 00:43:07,260
No one shall save you!

1237
00:43:07,260 --> 00:43:10,420
The shaman is trying to
seal me away.

1238
00:43:10,420 --> 00:43:13,020
I do not want to leave.

1239
00:43:13,020 --> 00:43:16,410
I have not met Gaysorn yet!

1240
00:43:17,860 --> 00:43:18,690
Gaysorn...?

1241
00:43:20,280 --> 00:43:21,240
Gaysorn...?

1242
00:43:22,210 --> 00:43:23,020
Gaysorn...

1243
00:43:26,210 --> 00:43:27,080
Danai?

1244
00:43:27,640 --> 00:43:28,990
It's really you.

1245
00:43:29,980 --> 00:43:30,900
Do you remember me?

1246
00:43:30,900 --> 00:43:31,780
I'm Tong.

1247
00:43:31,960 --> 00:43:33,460
The kid who lived next to your house.

1248
00:43:33,610 --> 00:43:34,450
Tong...

1249
00:43:35,440 --> 00:43:36,190
Tong,

1250
00:43:36,450 --> 00:43:37,390
son of Tor

1251
00:43:37,930 --> 00:43:38,730
and grandson of Toom,

1252
00:43:39,220 --> 00:43:40,360
who sold stoves in the market.

1253
00:43:40,520 --> 00:43:41,220
Tong,

1254
00:43:41,420 --> 00:43:43,200
who liked to fart in the tub.

1255
00:43:43,200 --> 00:43:45,140
After I got caught,

1256
00:43:45,140 --> 00:43:47,780
my father slapped me so hard
I pooped everywhere.

1257
00:43:47,780 --> 00:43:49,390
Yeah, that's enough.

1258
00:43:49,390 --> 00:43:50,590
The more you say it...

1259
00:43:51,260 --> 00:43:51,900
the more disgusting it gets.

1260
00:43:52,720 --> 00:43:54,130
Come here.

1261
00:43:54,820 --> 00:43:56,260
Wait, wait.

1262
00:43:56,400 --> 00:43:58,990
What about Toi, Tor's brother
and Ting's husband? Is he dead?

1263
00:43:59,130 --> 00:44:00,190
Tor and he died at the same time.

1264
00:44:00,190 --> 00:44:01,020
Tor...

1265
00:44:01,020 --> 00:44:02,100
Oh, don't do that!

1266
00:44:02,250 --> 00:44:03,410
Stop with all the alliterations.

1267
00:44:03,660 --> 00:44:04,410
I'm Tong.

1268
00:44:04,880 --> 00:44:06,000
Tong...

1269
00:44:06,560 --> 00:44:09,410
How did you end up
as a shaman?

1270
00:44:09,650 --> 00:44:11,930
Well, after you broke up
with Gaysorn

1271
00:44:12,050 --> 00:44:13,580
and were forced into a marriage,

1272
00:44:13,780 --> 00:44:15,410
you moved away.

1273
00:44:15,790 --> 00:44:17,590
I was forced

1274
00:44:17,620 --> 00:44:19,540
to study hard to become a medical student.

1275
00:44:19,540 --> 00:44:20,980
But I read from a wrong book.

1276
00:44:21,130 --> 00:44:22,380
I read from a book for
spiritual intermediaries.

1277
00:44:22,650 --> 00:44:23,730
So I ended up becoming
a spiritual healer,

1278
00:44:23,980 --> 00:44:25,390
- instead of a regular one.
- Is that why you are a shaman?

1279
00:44:25,390 --> 00:44:26,000
Yes.

1280
00:44:26,290 --> 00:44:27,060
Oh...

1281
00:44:27,060 --> 00:44:27,790
What about you?

1282
00:44:28,090 --> 00:44:30,560
Why are you a spirit
haunting this place?

1283
00:44:37,130 --> 00:44:38,440
If you guys really are friends,

1284
00:44:38,810 --> 00:44:40,420
why were you screaming in pain?

1285
00:44:40,780 --> 00:44:44,210
I wanted to know what it feels like

1286
00:44:44,420 --> 00:44:45,480
when sacred rice is thrown at you.

1287
00:44:45,480 --> 00:44:47,920
I saw it all the time in
those TV dramas, you know?

1288
00:44:48,060 --> 00:44:49,150
I wanted to know what it feels like.

1289
00:44:49,170 --> 00:44:49,770
Mm,

1290
00:44:49,800 --> 00:44:50,920
it is pretty effective.

1291
00:44:50,920 --> 00:44:52,710
It burned all over.

1292
00:44:52,990 --> 00:44:53,820
Oh...

1293
00:44:54,330 --> 00:44:55,390
I was so worried.

1294
00:44:55,600 --> 00:44:57,120
I thought you were defeated.

1295
00:45:00,190 --> 00:45:01,760
You were worried about me?

1296
00:45:07,060 --> 00:45:08,320
I wasn't worried.

1297
00:45:08,590 --> 00:45:09,600
I was irritated, alright?

1298
00:45:10,580 --> 00:45:11,260
Yeah...

1299
00:45:11,580 --> 00:45:13,280
You disappeared for a few days,

1300
00:45:13,960 --> 00:45:15,060
and I didn't know where you went.

1301
00:45:18,190 --> 00:45:19,610
I did not go anywhere.

1302
00:45:19,740 --> 00:45:21,240
I was just wandering around.

1303
00:45:21,650 --> 00:45:22,990
I did not want to show up,

1304
00:45:23,130 --> 00:45:24,440
because I was sick of you.

1305
00:45:24,440 --> 00:45:26,050
I do not want to see your face.

1306
00:45:26,200 --> 00:45:28,210
Just go already. Go.

1307
00:45:28,420 --> 00:45:29,180
Go!

1308
00:45:31,390 --> 00:45:31,920
Dobby.

1309
00:45:31,920 --> 00:45:32,420
Dobby, where are you going?

1310
00:45:32,420 --> 00:45:32,980
We came all the way here to help.

1311
00:45:32,980 --> 00:45:34,690
Is Gramps friends
with the shaman?

1312
00:45:35,900 --> 00:45:36,370
- Dobby.
- He left.

1313
00:45:36,570 --> 00:45:37,290
Tell me.

1314
00:45:37,310 --> 00:45:39,710
- Dobby.
- And they didn't even apologize.

1315
00:45:41,290 --> 00:45:42,540
It's a misunderstanding.

1316
00:45:42,540 --> 00:45:43,920
Danai, I don't understand.

1317
00:45:43,920 --> 00:45:45,790
Why didn't you just tell him

1318
00:45:45,920 --> 00:45:47,930
that you were gone because you went to

1319
00:45:47,930 --> 00:45:49,660
Nakhon Sawan to apologize to his mother?

1320
00:45:51,420 --> 00:45:52,180
I do not want all that trouble.

1321
00:45:52,820 --> 00:45:54,810
I do not want to argue with him.

1322
00:45:55,800 --> 00:45:57,040
Your grandson can hear you,

1323
00:45:57,790 --> 00:45:59,240
but you won't talk to him.

1324
00:46:00,020 --> 00:46:01,640
Your daughter can't hear you,

1325
00:46:01,840 --> 00:46:03,330
but you want to make it up to her, huh?

1326
00:46:03,600 --> 00:46:05,600
What do you want me to do?

1327
00:46:05,600 --> 00:46:06,190
Hm?

1328
00:46:06,420 --> 00:46:08,590
Confess to him?

1329
00:46:08,590 --> 00:46:09,580
Apologize to him and say,

1330
00:46:09,580 --> 00:46:10,990
"I am sorry

1331
00:46:11,220 --> 00:46:14,330
for trying to force your mother

1332
00:46:14,330 --> 00:46:17,410
to marry a degenerate like Surachet"?

1333
00:46:17,810 --> 00:46:20,760
If I did, he would spit in my face.

1334
00:46:21,180 --> 00:46:21,790
Danai,

1335
00:46:22,330 --> 00:46:25,010
is it that hard to admit you were wrong?

1336
00:46:25,390 --> 00:46:27,160
You know that it was your fault, don't you?

1337
00:46:27,790 --> 00:46:28,520
Yeah!

1338
00:46:28,700 --> 00:46:29,330
It was my fault.

1339
00:46:29,770 --> 00:46:31,000
I admit that I was wrong.

1340
00:46:31,720 --> 00:46:33,790
Are you satisfied now, Tong?!

1341
00:46:34,050 --> 00:46:34,990
Well, I am satisfied.

1342
00:46:36,010 --> 00:46:37,390
But I'm not the person

1343
00:46:37,900 --> 00:46:39,410
you should be saying this to.

1344
00:46:39,790 --> 00:46:41,280
Talk to your grandson.

1345
00:46:41,700 --> 00:46:42,890
I am not going to talk to him...

1346
00:46:43,200 --> 00:46:43,890
Ugh...

1347
00:46:44,820 --> 00:46:46,090
It is all in the past now.

1348
00:46:47,330 --> 00:46:50,080
She is living a happy life.

1349
00:46:50,080 --> 00:46:52,160
I just want to take this secret

1350
00:46:52,160 --> 00:46:55,160
to my grave.

1351
00:47:07,390 --> 00:47:08,590
Oh! That is hot!

1352
00:47:08,590 --> 00:47:09,410
You...!

1353
00:47:10,680 --> 00:47:11,410
Hey, Dobby...

1354
00:47:11,740 --> 00:47:12,810
Hey, what are you listening to?

1355
00:47:13,700 --> 00:47:14,590
What did Gramps say?

1356
00:47:14,860 --> 00:47:16,210
Hey, tell me.

1357
00:47:16,440 --> 00:47:17,360
Ugh, this is frustrating!

1358
00:47:17,360 --> 00:47:18,060
I want to hear it.

1359
00:47:18,060 --> 00:47:19,120
- I want to hear it, too.
- Hey.

1360
00:47:24,030 --> 00:47:26,720
Do you happen to have
a relative named Gaysorn?

1361
00:47:26,740 --> 00:47:27,830
Stop wasting my time.

1362
00:47:27,850 --> 00:47:29,110
How could you say that?!

1363
00:47:29,130 --> 00:47:30,960
He probably won't
waste his time talking to us.

1364
00:47:35,790 --> 00:47:36,360
Cut!

1365
00:47:37,390 --> 00:47:37,960
Cut.

1366
00:47:38,720 --> 00:47:39,920
These two were too slow.

1367
00:47:40,530 --> 00:47:40,930
Cut!

1368
00:47:40,960 --> 00:47:42,720
What even was that acting?!

1369
00:47:43,980 --> 00:47:44,590
You all.

1370
00:47:44,720 --> 00:47:45,490
You,

1371
00:47:45,520 --> 00:47:46,600
you, and you!

1372
00:47:46,620 --> 00:47:47,360
Director,

1373
00:47:47,380 --> 00:47:48,380
you should fire the entire crew.

1374
00:47:51,230 --> 00:47:54,670
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1375
00:47:54,830 --> 00:47:58,610
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1376
00:48:01,090 --> 00:48:06,570
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

1377
00:48:08,320 --> 00:48:13,020
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

1378
00:48:15,500 --> 00:48:21,640
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

1379
00:48:22,550 --> 00:48:27,120
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

1380
00:48:27,140 --> 00:48:30,650
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

1381
00:48:30,670 --> 00:48:34,250
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

1382
00:48:34,270 --> 00:48:37,790
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

1383
00:48:37,810 --> 00:48:40,160
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

1384
00:48:40,190 --> 00:48:46,510
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

1385
00:48:47,170 --> 00:48:53,900
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

1386
00:48:54,380 --> 00:49:01,530
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

1387
00:49:01,550 --> 00:49:08,470
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫

1388
00:49:08,490 --> 00:49:12,120
[The D Dorm]
